{"title":"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:50)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMthLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMthLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b1a3a99f948263840f88fe2fc1fea310ef4182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=n^3-5n^2+2n+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4729093fd7b46b5f37e798793bdaa99d168aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(n)=n^3-6n^2+5n+12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"21\" /> What is the sum of all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/4388be636eef1549fba122469c6ff28d19cffa99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{f(n)}{g(n)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"32\" height=\"29\" /> is an integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab195c074c73e0402c138770c6dbc690cdb4f4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~3\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~4\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~5\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fda49917e5cf30f3fdcf2fbf4ed52d62ab10fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> can be factored using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_root_theorem\" title=\"Rational root theorem\">rational root theorem</a>. By trying out a few values, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56584f0779cf04f3f0d66161f78cb2175bd832c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />. Then, we can use synthetic division (regular polynomial division works, too) to get the other roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />, which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Now we factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fda49917e5cf30f3fdcf2fbf4ed52d62ab10fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. By inspection, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56584f0779cf04f3f0d66161f78cb2175bd832c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> also works on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fda49917e5cf30f3fdcf2fbf4ed52d62ab10fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, and so synthetic division and factoring the remaining quadratic gets us the roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/827ad4873f29fdb4bccd7d4b2e022eb3143e42af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> We can now express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c34d5e56f67e60fc487f6a5fd1cce19efde80873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(n)}{g(n)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"42\" height=\"45\" /> as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/0022f9607ccc217c31ad33ea79c0cd5a42d89975.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(n + 1)(n - 4)(n - 2)}{(n + 1)(n - 4)(n - 3)}.\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"43\" /> We can cancel the top and bottom to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba611f6aeb3b4a8d0e4f0a5e81f396103ab33f35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n - 2}{n - 3}.\\]\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p>Notice that the only values for which this expression is an integer are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, because they both cause the denominator to have a magnitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is an extraneous solution as plugging it back into the original expression would make it evaluate to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d7ada08ad200c068f7060c22ead4ad2e1a2e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{0}{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Our answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f5670ff2ccb7f7dbe7c24c90da636996d6a4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Milkdrinker and SixthGradeBookWorm927\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9633c682d4b9d54e7cb65d2e1af84631192999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(n)}{g(n)} = \\frac{n^3-5n^2+2n+8}{n^3-6n^2+5n+12} = 1 + \\frac{n^2-3n-4}{n^3-6n^2+5n+12}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"436\" height=\"45\" /> We factor the numerator as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/54654a40a9b0498647c70ef290255ee6d2503b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-4)(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />. Using synthetic division on the numerator's roots to factor the denominator, we find that the denominator is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a51222801d8f07d30ffa4c3d6a205c052f81209b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)(n-3)(n-4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d641fe757585ced81f1ae0ebf08302f2b573d08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(n)}{g(n)} = 1 + \\frac{1}{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"143\" height=\"45\" />. However, we <i>must not</i> include the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee40a8ce75c2afd4aec32bae7c14f947cf80c0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=-1, 3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or the original fraction will be undefined.\n</p><p>To have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7de119d128ea531ac57b98d96b7f3d27f691410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"40\" /> be an integer, we require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfa2f2fec130acbac86c7eb1e1c19435b060a5a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. This would give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but as in Solution 1, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> must not be included, we deduce that there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f5670ff2ccb7f7dbe7c24c90da636996d6a4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~OlympiadMaster\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have to plug in different values into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9633c682d4b9d54e7cb65d2e1af84631192999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(n)}{g(n)} = \\frac{n^3-5n^2+2n+8}{n^3-6n^2+5n+12} = 1 + \\frac{n^2-3n-4}{n^3-6n^2+5n+12}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"436\" height=\"45\" /> Because of the answer choices, we only really need to test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging in each of these values leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/135624b30829ac9199e326d1dcbb67cd16eeadc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"93\" height=\"30\" /> as our answer, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is the only value that leads to an integer. Note that plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b5f8a01adc0144788a9c0848dce9646f7b55837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0/0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />, which is undefined.\n</p><p>~ AskNamanonyt\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:50.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:50)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:50)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/TqS0hUTveSI\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/TqS0hUTveSI</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cfYdgea3oDQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cfYdgea3oDQ</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMthLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMthLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMthLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hFWxfehU_Qo&amp;t=3s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hFWxfehU_Qo&amp;t=3s</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline